---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Manifesto | Practical Humanism">
	<section class="manifesto-content">
		<h1>Manifesto</h1>
		
		<blockquote class="lead-quote">
			"Man is a transitional being, he is not final; for in him and high beyond him ascend the radiant degrees which climb to a divine supermanhood." 
			<cite>— Sri Aurobindo</cite>
		</blockquote>

		<p class="intro-text">
			I stand where the Ageless Wisdom intersects with the exactitudes of modern logic. 
			What I term <strong>Practical Humanism</strong> is no mere philosophical speculation; 
			it is a definite, pragmatic Method for the deliberate unfolding of human potential.
		</p>

		<div class="manifesto-section">
			<h2>The Law of Transition</h2>
			<p>
				I recognize that the present human form is not an ultimate completion, but an intermediate stage. 
				The individual is the living bridge between the mechanical past and the radiant destiny of the True Self. 
				My aim is to hasten this Great Work, passing consciously from the bondage of automatic reaction into the mastery of deliberate creation.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="manifesto-section">
			<h2>The Synergetic Instruments</h2>
			<p>
				I cast aside nothing of the ancient tools; rather, I adapt them to present necessities. 
				Meditation, deliberate visualization, and concentrated contemplation are not relics of a dead past—they are the exact sciences of consciousness. 
				The Tarot, the Qabalah, and Yoga are not superstitions; they are precise blueprints of the inner constitution of Man. 
				By applying these traditional instruments with a strictly practical, testing attitude, I aim to awaken the dormant centers of the personality.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="manifesto-section">
			<h2>The Ultimate Aim</h2>
			<p>
				To make of my own vehicle a living laboratory of evolution. The Work demands the balanced development of the entire being: 
				the purification of the mental body, the direction of the Will, and the conscious realization of the Indwelling Spirit. 
				I take up the tools of the Builder, knowing that I am the sole architect of my own ascent.
			</p>
		</div>

		<hr />
	</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.manifesto-content {
		max-width: 700px;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}
	.lead-quote {
		margin: 3rem 0;
		font-size: 1.4rem;
		line-height: 1.4;
		border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-color);
		padding-left: 2rem;
	}
	.lead-quote cite {
		display: block;
		margin-top: 1rem;
		font-size: 1rem;
		font-style: normal;
		color: var(--accent-muted);
		font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
	}
	.intro-text {
		font-size: 1.2rem;
		line-height: 1.8;
		margin-bottom: 4rem;
		color: var(--text-color);
	}
	.manifesto-section {
		margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
	}
	.manifesto-section h2 {
		color: var(--accent-color);
		letter-spacing: 0.05em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		font-size: 1.4rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-color);
		display: inline-block;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}
	.manifesto-section p {
		line-height: 1.8;
	}

	@media (max-width: 768px) {
		.lead-quote {
			font-size: 1.2rem;
			padding-left: 1.5rem;
		}
		.intro-text {
			font-size: 1.1rem;
		}
		.manifesto-section h2 {
			font-size: 1.2rem;
		}
	}
</style>
